---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
import FoveationExplorer from '../components/FoveationExplorer.astro';
import PlanFigure from '../components/PlanFigure.astro';
import Proof from '../components/Proof.astro';
import FrameworkTabs from '../components/FrameworkTabs.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const roadmap = await getEntry('docs', 'docs/roadmap');
const upcoming = (roadmap?.data.items ?? []).filter((i) => i.status === 'building').slice(0, 4);
---
<Landing
  title="Foveate: put the right pages in the window, and prove the answer"
  description="Context engineering for LLM apps. Foveate picks the pages that matter, keeps the rest as an outline, and checks every citation against the source."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Context engineering for LLM apps</p>
        <h1>Put the right pages in the window. <em>Prove the answer.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Foveate reads a long document the way an eye reads a scene: sharp on what matters, coarse on the rest. It picks the pages for your question, sends the rest as an outline, and checks every quote in the answer against the page it names.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href={`${base}docs/quickstart/`}>Start in five minutes</a>
          <a class="btn" href={`${base}docs/learn/context-engineering/`}>New to context engineering?</a>
        </div>
        <div class="install"><code>pip install "foveate[pdf]"</code><button type="button" data-copy='pip install "foveate[pdf]"' aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="visual">
        <PlanFigure />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Proof />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <h2>What happens when you upload 200 pages</h2>
        <p>Three common outcomes. Only the last one gives you something you can check.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="trio">
        <article>
          <span class="n">01</span>
          <h3>Send everything</h3>
          <p>If the file is larger than the model's window it fails or is silently cut. If it fits, every question costs tens of thousands of tokens, and models read the middle of a long prompt least reliably.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="n">02</span>
          <h3>Add plain retrieval</h3>
          <p>Cheaper, but the model gets loose chunks with no page numbers. Nothing checks the answer, and a question the file cannot answer still gets an answer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="hl">
          <span class="n">03</span>
          <h3>Foveate</h3>
          <p>The relevant pages arrive in full, their neighbours in short, the rest as a one-line outline. The answer cites page and quote, each quote is checked, and a missing answer is reported as missing.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="explore">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">See it</p>
        <h2>What the model would receive</h2>
        <p>Real plans for three questions on real filings, computed by the library with no model call. Move the budget and watch the pages change. The green ring marks the page that holds the answer; at small budgets it is sometimes missed, and that is shown honestly.</p>
      </div>
      <FoveationExplorer />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Six decisions, each one inspectable</h2>
        <p>Context engineering is the set of choices about what goes in the prompt. Foveate makes each one explicit.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Select</h3><p>Rank pages for this question with keywords, embeddings or both. <a href={`${base}docs/learn/selection/`}>Selection</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>Shape</h3><p>Full, condensed or outline: each page gets the detail it deserves within your budget. <a href={`${base}docs/learn/foveation/`}>Foveation</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>Compress</h3><p>Shrink chat history and tool output, mostly without a model. <a href={`${base}docs/learn/compression/`}>Compression</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>Remember</h3><p>Session notes and durable facts, recalled by relevance. <a href={`${base}docs/learn/memory/`}>Memory</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>Verify</h3><p>Cite page and quote, check the quote in code, retry or refuse. <a href={`${base}docs/learn/grounding/`}>Grounding</a></p></li>
        <li><h3>Measure</h3><p>Test on your own documents before you trust anyone's numbers. <a href={`${base}docs/guides/evaluating/`}>Evaluating</a></p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap two">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Learn</p>
        <h2>A playbook for people new to this</h2>
        <p class="lede">Twelve rules, one page each: the problem in plain words, why it happens, what to do, a worked example and the mistakes to avoid. Written from the research and from teams that run agents in production.</p>
        <div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href={`${base}docs/playbook/`}>Read the playbook</a></div>
      </div>
      <ul class="rules" aria-label="The twelve rules">
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/01-measure-first/`}><span>1</span>Measure first</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/02-send-less/`}><span>2</span>Send less, not more</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/03-edges/`}><span>3</span>Best evidence at the edges</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/04-stable-prefixes/`}><span>4</span>Keep prefixes stable</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/05-trim-first/`}><span>5</span>Trim before you summarise</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/06-clear-tool-output/`}><span>6</span>Clear old tool output</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/07-just-in-time/`}><span>7</span>Pull context just in time</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/08-memory/`}><span>8</span>Two kinds of memory</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/09-cite-and-verify/`}><span>9</span>Cite, then verify</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/10-abstain/`}><span>10</span>Abstain when evidence is missing</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/11-fence-untrusted-text/`}><span>11</span>Fence untrusted text</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}docs/playbook/12-room/`}><span>12</span>Tell the model its room</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Agents</p>
        <h2>Works with the framework you already use</h2>
        <p>Foveate depends on no agent framework. Small adapter packages give your agent page tools and a history budget in a few lines.</p>
      </div>
      <FrameworkTabs />
      <ul class="facts">
        <li><strong>No SDKs.</strong> Talks to any OpenAI-compatible server (OpenAI, vLLM, Ollama, NVIDIA, Together) with the standard library.</li>
        <li><strong>Reliable.</strong> Cache, retries, circuit breaker, rate limits, and recovery when a reasoning model spends its whole token cap thinking.</li>
        <li><strong>Observable.</strong> Typed events and OpenTelemetry spans. Python 3.10 to 3.13 on Linux, macOS and Windows.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap honest">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Honesty</p>
        <h2>Where it does not win</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>We publish the results that do not favour Foveate. On the same questions, plain retrieval found hidden sentences in long pages that Foveate missed, Foveate sent more tokens than plain retrieval, and it gave the same answer to reworded questions less often. Better retrieval put the evidence page in the prompt much more often but did not raise accuracy. No pipeline solved needles that share no words with the question.</p>
        <p>Thirty questions and one model is a small sample. Run the harness on your own documents before you trust any of this.</p>
        <a class="btn" href={`${base}evidence/`}>See every result</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Coming next</p>
        <h2>What we are building</h2>
        <p>The gaps the benchmarks found, in the order we are closing them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        {upcoming.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="chip building">Being built</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{item.summary}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a href={`${base}roadmap/`}>See the full roadmap</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start with a dry run</h2>
      <p class="lede">Plan a question on your own file with no model and no cost. Then ask it, with citations.</p>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href={`${base}docs/quickstart/`}>Open the quickstart</a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/sachncs/foveate">View on GitHub</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? '');
          button.textContent = 'Copied';
          setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy'), 1800);
        } catch {
          button.textContent = 'Press Ctrl+C';
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</Landing>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 7rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.12fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent-text); }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .install { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: .45rem .5rem .45rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: 999px; max-width: 100%; background: var(--surface); }
  .install code { font-size: .84rem; overflow-x: auto; white-space: nowrap; }
  .install button { border: 0; background: var(--text); color: var(--bg); border-radius: 999px; padding: .45rem .95rem; font: inherit; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 560; cursor: pointer; min-height: 32px; }
  section.tight { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .trio { display: grid; gap: 0; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .trio { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .trio article { padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-8) var(--space-8) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); position: relative; }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .trio article { border-bottom: 0; border-right: 1px solid var(--border); padding-left: var(--space-8); } .trio article:first-child { padding-left: 0; } .trio article:last-child { border-right: 0; padding-right: 0; } }
  .trio .n { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--muted); display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .trio h3 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.9rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .trio p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .98rem; }
  .trio .hl h3 { color: var(--accent-text); }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 0; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); counter-reset: s; }
  .steps li { counter-increment: s; padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-6) var(--space-8) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(s, decimal-leading-zero); display: block; font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--muted); font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .steps h3 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .steps p { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .two { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .two { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .rules { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); gap: 0 var(--space-6); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .rules li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .rules a { display: flex; gap: .9rem; align-items: baseline; padding: .8rem 0; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 520; }
  .rules a:hover { color: var(--accent-text); }
  .rules span { font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; min-width: 1.4rem; }
  .facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--space-12) 0 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-6); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); }
  .facts li { color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; padding-top: var(--space-4); border-top: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .facts strong { color: var(--text); display: block; margin-bottom: .25rem; }
  .honest { display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .honest { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); } }
  .prose { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .prose .btn { justify-self: start; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .more { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .card h3 { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .card p { margin-top: var(--space-2); font-size: .95rem; }
  .final { text-align: center; }
  .final .lede { margin-inline: auto; }
  .final .cta { justify-content: center; }
</style>
